---
export const prerender = false;
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '~/components/Footer.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy · Kazon Wilson" description="How this website handles contact messages, audio inquiries, resume requests, and information used to keep the site working.">
  <article class="site-shell py-16">
    <div class="max-w-measure">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4">Updated September 19, 2026</p>
      <h1 class="display mb-6">Privacy</h1>
      <p>This is Kazon Wilson’s website, operated through The Superhuman Group LLC. This notice covers thesuperhuman.us and its audio pages.</p>
      <h2>Information you send</h2>
      <p>Contact messages, audio inquiries, and resume requests include the details you enter, such as your name, email address, company, and message or project information. These details are used to respond to you, discuss potential work, or review your resume request. Resume delivery requires my approval.</p>
      <h2>Services that process information</h2>
      <p>Cloudflare hosts and protects the site. Its Turnstile service processes browser and network signals to prevent automated form abuse. Resend delivers form notifications and requested emails. Your browser also contacts Google Fonts to load the site’s typefaces.</p>
      <p>Read the providers’ privacy information: <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/policies/privacy/">Cloudflare</a>, <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/">Turnstile</a>, <a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy">Resend</a>, and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google</a>.</p>
      <h2>Storage and retention</h2>
      <p>Pending resume requests expire from the website’s request store after seven days and are removed when processed. Temporary IP-based form rate-limit records expire after five minutes. These limits do not delete email copies. Messages and provider logs have separate retention settings; contact me about a specific message or deletion request.</p>
      <h2>Cookies and site operation</h2>
      <p>The site uses hosting and security services to serve pages and investigate failures. The private publishing sign-in uses a short-lived security cookie. The website’s page code does not include advertising trackers. Music pages collect the limited playback information described below.</p>
      <h2>Music and audio projects</h2>
      <p>Music pages record playback starts, progress, 30 seconds of audible listening, completion, and replay. Random identifiers in your browser’s tab storage keep events in order and reduce duplicate counting. Campaign, channel, and creative labels in a link may also be stored so I can compare promotion results. These records describe reported playthroughs, not verified people or audited unique listeners.</p>
      <p>Cloudflare may provide an approximate country, region, and city with a playback request. The site stores that approximation with the event, but does not store the request IP address in the music database. City patterns appear in the private owner view only after at least five qualifying reported sessions share a city. That threshold reduces exposure; it does not prove that five different people listened.</p>
      <p>Individual playback records are reviewed after 90 days. After reviewing a summary, I can remove those records through a manual cleanup. Daily playback totals and privacy-thresholded geography may be retained to understand longer-term interest. Cleanup is not automatic, so individual records may remain longer than 90 days.</p>
      <p>If you request a song or merchandise, the site stores your email, choices, and optional suggestion so I can follow up about that request. This does not create an order or subscribe you to a newsletter. Contact me to withdraw your request or ask for deletion.</p>
      <p>Audio project requests include the file-sharing links and creative notes you provide. Share only files you want me to review. A YouTube lyric video connects to YouTube when you choose to load it; YouTube then handles playback under Google’s privacy policy.</p>
      <h2>Questions or requests</h2>
      <p>To ask about information you have submitted, request access or correction, or request deletion, email <a href="mailto:kazon.wilson@thesuperhuman.us">kazon.wilson@thesuperhuman.us</a>. Include enough context to identify your message without sending sensitive documents.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
  <Footer compact slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.2; margin-block: 2rem .75rem; }
  p { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  a { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
